// Title: Python Spawning Pretty TTY Via PTY Module
// Sigma ID: c4042d54-110d-45dd-a0e1-05c47822c937
// Status: test | Level: medium
// Author: Nextron Systems
// Date: 2022-06-03 | Modified: 2024-11-04
// ATT&CK: execution, T1059
// Description: Detects a python process calling to the PTY module in order to spawn a pretty tty which could be
//   indicative of potential reverse shell activity.
// False positives:
//   - Unknown
// References:
//   - https://www.volexity.com/blog/2022/06/02/zero-day-exploitation-of-atlassian-confluence/
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/05d1031f537e830b76da53bae2400c5814c89165/rules/linux/process_creation/proc_creation_lnx_python_pty_spawn.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where ((FolderPath endswith "/python" or FolderPath endswith "/python2" or FolderPath endswith "/python3") or (FolderPath contains "/python2." or FolderPath contains "/python3.")) and (ProcessCommandLine contains "import pty" or ProcessCommandLine contains "from pty ") and ProcessCommandLine contains "spawn"
